  <body>
    <sec>
      <title>Cutaneous findings</title>
      <p>Cutaneous manifestations are among the most frequent findings and are
      illustrated in <xref ref-type="fig" rid="f1 f2">Figures 1 and 2</xref>.
      This intentionally long sentence exists so that the paragraph as a whole
      exceeds six hundred characters of running text before and after the
      figure reference, which lets the parser exercise its trimmed window
      behaviour around the first matching cross-reference rather than storing
      the entire paragraph. Additional filler text keeps going so the window
      really does have to be applied in practice and the resulting mention is
      meaningfully shorter than the source paragraph while still containing
      the reference itself.</p>
      <p>The malar rash is shown again in <xref ref-type="fig" rid="f1">Figure 1</xref> with discussion.</p>
    </sec>
    <sec>
      <title>Diagnosis</title>
      <p>Diagnostic criteria are summarized in <xref ref-type="fig" rid="f3">Figure 3</xref>.</p>
    </sec>
